## llama.cpp

Real inference comes from [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)
by Georgi Gerganov and contributors, MIT licensed. No llama.cpp source is
committed here: enabling the `llama-cpp` feature pulls the
[`llama-cpp-2`](https://crates.io/crates/llama-cpp-2) bindings (also MIT) from
crates.io, and those bindings fetch and compile the C++ library as part of the
build, with Metal back ends added by that library's own build system where the
toolchain supports them. Every shipped CI build uses the `mock` engine instead,
so a released binary contains llama.cpp only if you built it yourself with
`--features llama-cpp`.

The GGUF format llama.cpp defines is what this app reads; model metadata parsing
and the tensor-accurate memory estimates are built on that format, not on llama
.cpp's own headers being available at write time.

## Inter

The UI ships two self-hosted font files,
`desktop/src/assets/fonts/inter-latin-wght.woff2` and `inter-latin-ext-wght.woff2`,
copied from the `@fontsource-variable/inter` package
([Inter Project Authors](https://github.com/rsms/inter), Copyright 2016) under
the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
The full licence text is committed next to the fonts as
[INTER-LICENSE.txt](desktop/src/assets/fonts/INTER-LICENSE.txt) and must stay
there. Only the `latin` and `latin-ext` subsets of the variable weight axis are
vendored; no glyph data is modified, and the files are served from the app's own
origin rather than a font CDN, which is also why the Content-Security-Policy can
restrict `font-src` to `'self'`.

## The Rust and npm dependency tree

Tauri 2 and its plugins (`dialog`, `window-state`), Axum, Tokio, reqwest,
serde, tracing, sysinfo, `keyring`, React, TanStack Query, Radix UI and
Tailwind are used under their own licences, the large majority MIT or
Apache-2.0. Exact versions are pinned in `Cargo.lock` and
`desktop/pnpm-lock.yaml`, so the set a given build used is reproducible from
that build's source. None of them phone home; the app's own outbound requests
are documented in [docs/privacy.md](docs/privacy.md).

## Model files

This repository publishes no weights. The catalog points at files hosted by
[Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co), and each model arrives under its own
licence — `apache-2.0`, MIT, Llama, Gemma and other community terms all appear
in the catalog. Those licences are the reason the Models page shows a licence on
every entry, and they are the terms that govern what you may do with a model;
SmolLLM Studio's MIT licence says nothing about them. Read the licence on the
model's own page before you distribute an output or a fine-tune built on it.

